      "content": "got it. so basically the old money side is centered on that western european classical look, while the urban side is where we lean into more diverse, multicultural energy. \n\nto help the marketing team with the moodboards, could you go a bit deeper into the 'vibe' of the people in those two groups? specifically, if we were describing their level of sophistication or their 'social standing' in a campaign text, how would you differentiate them? i want to make sure we don't accidentally make the urban group seem too 'low-brow' or the old money group seem too 'stiff,' but you know, we still need to capture that inherent difference in their social class and cultural polish.",
